<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="box-dimensions">
    <title>Box dimensions</title>
    <shortdesc><xref href="../glossaries/CSS.dita">CSS</xref> sizing properties set preferred dimensions or place minimum and maximum limits on them. They apply to CSS boxes, not directly to <xref href="../glossaries/XML.dita">XML</xref> tags. Select an element from your XML, then use the property that matches the dimension or limit you need.</shortdesc>
    <conbody>
        <p>For the meaning of CSS boxes and the length units used below, see <xref href="box-sizing-and-spacing.dita#box-sizing-and-spacing">Box sizing, margins and padding</xref>.</p>
        <p>These properties also accept the CSS-wide keywords. See <xref href="inheritance-and-defaults.dita#inheritance-and-defaults">Inheritance and default values</xref>.</p>
        <p>CSSMedia parses these declarations and computes their style values, but it does not lay out element boxes or generate a <xref href="../glossaries/PDF.dita">PDF</xref>. The properties therefore do not affect PDF output. The <codeph>Default</codeph> cells below and in the <xref href="../references/dimension-properties.dita#dimension-properties">dimension property reference</xref> are left blank because there is no PDF output. The <codeph>Values</codeph> entries describe CSS syntax. <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-anchor-position-1/#funcdef-anchor-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Anchor Positioning</xref> defines <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph> for physical sizing properties, not their logical counterparts.</p>
        <section id="preferred-sizes">
            <title>Preferred sizes</title>
            <p>
                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#specifying-sizes" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3 §3, Specifying Box Sizes</xref>; <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-logical-1/#dimension-properties" scope="external" format="html">CSS Logical Properties 1 §4.1, Logical Height and Logical Width</xref>.</p>
            <p>
                <codeph>width</codeph> and <codeph>height</codeph> refer to the physical axes. <codeph>inline-size</codeph> and <codeph>block-size</codeph> refer to the text’s inline and block axes. Their physical direction follows <codeph>writing-mode</codeph>.</p>
            <table id="box-dimensions__I_1i_">
                <tgroup cols="5">
                    <thead>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry align="center">Name</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Description</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Values</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Default</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Specification</entry>
                        </row>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-width" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>width</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets the preferred width of a box.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage [0,∞]&gt;)</codeph>, <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>, or <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-width" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-height" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>height</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets the preferred height of a box.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage [0,∞]&gt;)</codeph>, <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>, or <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-height" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-inline-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>inline-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets the preferred size along the inline axis.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content()</codeph>, or <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-inline-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-block-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>block-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets the preferred size along the block axis.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content()</codeph>, or <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-block-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                    </tbody>
                </tgroup>
            </table>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph> means a length such as <codeph>12pt</codeph>, a percentage such as <codeph>60%</codeph>, or a <codeph>calc()</codeph> expression combining them.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <codeph>[0,∞]</codeph> in <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage [0,∞]&gt;)</codeph> means the length or percentage cannot be negative.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>The <codeph>fit-content()</codeph> and <codeph>calc-size()</codeph> functions are defined in <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#sizing-values" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4 §3.2</xref>.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#valdef-width-auto" scope="external" format="html">
                            <codeph>auto</codeph>
                        </xref> lets the layout algorithm determine the size.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#valdef-width-min-content" scope="external" format="html">
                            <codeph>min-content</codeph>
                        </xref> uses the smallest size the content can take without avoidable overflow.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#valdef-width-max-content" scope="external" format="html">
                            <codeph>max-content</codeph>
                        </xref> uses the size the content would take without soft wrapping.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#valdef-width-fit-content" scope="external" format="html">
                            <codeph>fit-content</codeph>
                        </xref> fits the content within available space, bounded by its min-content and max-content sizes.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#funcdef-width-fit-content" scope="external" format="html">
                            <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage&gt;)</codeph>
                        </xref> uses the supplied non-negative length or percentage as the available-space limit.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#stretch-fit-size" scope="external" format="html">
                            <codeph>stretch</codeph>
                        </xref> sizes the margin box to fill the available space in that axis.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#valdef-width-contain" scope="external" format="html">
                            <codeph>contain</codeph>
                        </xref> uses contain-fit sizing. It fills the available space while preserving a preferred aspect ratio when one exists.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#funcdef-width-calc-size" scope="external" format="html">
                            <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>
                        </xref> calculates a size from an intrinsic-size basis. The basis can be an intrinsic keyword, another <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>, <codeph>any</codeph>, or a calculation. The second argument is a calculation using that basis.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-anchor-position-1/#funcdef-anchor-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>
                            </xref> accepts an optional anchor name, an optional size keyword, or both, followed by an optional length or percentage fallback. Its size keyword can be <codeph>width</codeph>, <codeph>height</codeph>, <codeph>block</codeph>, <codeph>inline</codeph>, <codeph>self-block</codeph> or <codeph>self-inline</codeph>. The function is for absolutely positioned boxes.</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>A percentage size is relative to the corresponding dimension of the containing block. The allowed length and percentage forms are described in <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-values-4/#percentages" scope="external" format="html">CSS Values 4 §5.5</xref> and <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-values-4/#lengths" scope="external" format="html">§6</xref>.</p>
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>For example, if your XML contains a <codeph>chapter</codeph> element and a <codeph>figure</codeph> inside it, these rules request a 30em inline size for the chapter and a 60 percent inline size for the figure:</p>
            <pre outputclass="language-xml">&lt;chapter&gt;
    &lt;figure&gt;Figure description and content.&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/chapter&gt;
</pre>
            <pre outputclass="language-css21">chapter {
    inline-size: 30em;
}

figure {
    inline-size: 60%;
    block-size: fit-content;
}
</pre>
            <p>Replace the example element names with names from your XML. If your document uses a vertical writing mode, inline and block dimensions map to different physical directions.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="minimum-and-maximum-sizes">
            <title>Minimum and maximum sizes</title>
            <p>
                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#specifying-sizes" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3 §3, Specifying Box Sizes</xref>; <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#sizing-properties" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4 §3.1, Sizing Properties</xref>; <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-logical-1/#dimension-properties" scope="external" format="html">CSS Logical Properties 1 §4.1</xref>.</p>
            <p>Minimum sizes set a lower limit. Maximum sizes set an upper limit. The layout algorithm applies the limits to the preferred size.</p>
            <table id="box-dimensions__I_1k_">
                <tgroup cols="5">
                    <thead>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry align="center">Name</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Description</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Values</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Default</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Specification</entry>
                        </row>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-min-width" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>min-width</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets a lower limit for the width.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage [0,∞]&gt;)</codeph>, <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>, or <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-min-width" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-min-height" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>min-height</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets a lower limit for the height.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage [0,∞]&gt;)</codeph>, <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>, or <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-min-height" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-min-inline-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>min-inline-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets a lower limit along the inline axis.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content()</codeph>, or <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-min-inline-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-min-block-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>min-block-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets a lower limit along the block axis.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content()</codeph>, or <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-min-block-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-max-width" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>max-width</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets an upper limit for the width.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <codeph>none</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage [0,∞]&gt;)</codeph>, <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>, or <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-max-width" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-max-height" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>max-height</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets an upper limit for the height.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <codeph>none</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage [0,∞]&gt;)</codeph>, <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>, or <codeph>anchor-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-max-height" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-max-inline-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>max-inline-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets an upper limit along the inline axis.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <codeph>none</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content()</codeph>, or <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-max-inline-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-max-block-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>max-block-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets an upper limit along the block axis.</entry>
                            <entry>
                                <codeph>none</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>stretch</codeph>, <codeph>contain</codeph>, <codeph>min-content</codeph>, <codeph>max-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content</codeph>, <codeph>fit-content()</codeph>, or <codeph>calc-size()</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-3/#propdef-max-block-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 3</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                    </tbody>
                </tgroup>
            </table>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <codeph>&lt;length-percentage&gt;</codeph> means a length such as <codeph>12pt</codeph>, a percentage such as <codeph>60%</codeph>, or a <codeph>calc()</codeph> expression combining them.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <codeph>[0,∞]</codeph> in <codeph>fit-content(&lt;length-percentage [0,∞]&gt;)</codeph> means the length or percentage cannot be negative.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <codeph>auto</codeph> on a minimum size lets the layout mode choose its automatic minimum. <codeph>none</codeph> on a maximum size means there is no maximum limit.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>For example, <codeph>max-inline-size</codeph> prevents a wide illustration from exceeding <codeph>40em</codeph>, while <codeph>inline-size: 100%</codeph> lets it use the containing block’s full inline size when there is room:</p>
                </li>
            </ul>
            <pre outputclass="language-xml">&lt;illustration&gt;Diagram of the assembly.&lt;/illustration&gt;
</pre>
            <pre outputclass="language-css21">illustration {
    inline-size: 100%;
    max-inline-size: 40em;
}
</pre>
            <div outputclass="role-h3" id="paired-size-shorthands">Paired size shorthands</div>
            <p>
                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#sizing-properties" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4 §3.1, Sizing Properties</xref>.</p>
            <table id="box-dimensions__I_1l_">
                <tgroup cols="5">
                    <thead>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry align="center">Name</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Description</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Values</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Default</entry>
                            <entry align="center">Specification</entry>
                        </row>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets both the preferred width and height.</entry>
                            <entry>One or two space-separated values. One value sets both dimensions; two set width then height.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-min-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>min-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets the minimum width and height.</entry>
                            <entry>One or two space-separated values. One value sets both dimensions; two set width then height.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-min-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row valign="middle">
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-max-size" scope="external" format="html">
                                    <codeph>max-size</codeph>
                                </xref>
                            </entry>
                            <entry>Sets the maximum width and height.</entry>
                            <entry>One or two space-separated values. One value sets both dimensions; two set width then height.</entry>
                            <entry />
                            <entry>
                                <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-max-size" scope="external" format="html">CSS Sizing 4</xref>
                            </entry>
                        </row>
                    </tbody>
                </tgroup>
            </table>
            <ul>
                <li>Each shorthand accepts one or two space-separated values. One value applies to both dimensions. Two values set width then height. Each value uses the grammar of its corresponding longhand.</li>
                <li>For <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-aspect-ratio" scope="external" format="html">
                        <codeph>aspect-ratio</codeph>
                    </xref>, the <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#intrinsic-sizes" scope="external" format="html">
                        <codeph>contain-intrinsic-*</codeph>
                    </xref> properties, <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-frame-sizing" scope="external" format="html">
                        <codeph>frame-sizing</codeph>
                    </xref>, and <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-sizing-4/#propdef-min-intrinsic-sizing" scope="external" format="html">
                        <codeph>min-intrinsic-sizing</codeph>
                    </xref>, see the <xref href="../references/dimension-properties.dita#dimension-properties">complete dimension property reference</xref>.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
    </conbody>
</concept>

